# SPA fallback, in the format Netlify and Cloudflare Pages both understand.
#
# The shop uses real paths (/p/netflix), so a shared link asks the host for a
# file that does not exist. Serve the app instead and let the router resolve it.
#
# Status 200, not 301: a redirect would change the address bar and lose the page
# the customer was sent.
#
# Prerendered pages (dist/p/netflix/index.html and the rest) are real files and
# are served before this rule is ever consulted — which is the point, because
# those carry the per-page title and description a crawler reads.
/*    /index.html   200
